<title>UK: Severn Trent sees debt rise on windfall tax.</title>
<headline>Severn Trent sees debt rise on windfall tax.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Water company Severn Trent Plc said on Thursday the British government's new windfall tax on utilities would force it to take on higher levels of debt to pay the levy.</p>
<p>&quot;The levy will undoubtedly impact on our business, particularly in servicing the increased levels of debt that we will need to take on in order to pay it,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
</text>
